This is the file. `health_check` being public is intended, but `get_profile` should NOT be reachable without a token.

You're right, don't hand-roll it. Look at the decorators: you wrote `walker :pub get_profile`. In Jac, `:pub` is exactly what makes a walker reachable with no JWT. The comment even says "Protected (default) -- requires JWT token", but the code marks it `:pub`, contradicting the comment. Protected is the *default*, so you get it by writing no visibility marker at all. Drop the `:pub`:

