    root ++> Person(name="Bob", age=25);
    root ++> Person(name="Carol", age=30);

    result = root spawn FindFirst();
    print(f"First adult: {result.reports[0].name}");
}
```

`result.reports` is empty so `result.reports[0].name` crashes.

Exactly, it's not the disengage or the filter, it's that the walker never reaches a Person. In `start` you have `visit [<--]`, following *incoming* edges of root; nothing points into root so the walk ends immediately with no visits. The Person nodes are on outgoing edges (`root ++> Person(...)`). Change it to `[-->]`:

```jac
node Person {
    has name: str;
    has age: int;
}

walker FindFirst {
    can start with Root entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can check with Person entry {
        if here.age >= 18 {
            report here;
            disengage;  # Stop immediately -- don't visit more nodes
        }
        visit [-->];
    }
}

with entry {
    root ++> Person(name="Alice", age=15);
    root ++> Person(name="Bob", age=25);
    root ++> Person(name="Carol", age=30);

    result = root spawn FindFirst();
    print(f"First adult: {result.reports[0].name}");
}
```

Now root visits Alice (15, skipped), then Bob (25, reported, then disengage), so `result.reports[0].name` is 'Bob'.

