Declaring two fields on an object and it won't compile:

```jac
obj Person {
    has name: str
        height: int = 0; # Declare all expected fields
}

with entry {
    p = Person(name="Alice", height=175);
    print(p.height);
}
```

The error is between the `name` and `height` fields.

Each field should be its own statement -- terminate the first one with a semicolon:

```jac
has name: str;
    height: int = 0;
```

Right -- that's because these are meant to be a single `has` clause listing multiple fields, which are separated by commas, not semicolons. The `;` only terminates the *last* field. Use a comma after `name`:

```jac
obj Person {
    has name: str,
        height: int = 0; # Declare all expected fields
}

with entry {
    p = Person(name="Alice", height=175);
    print(p.height);
}
```

