Right, `report` collects but doesn't move the walker -- you need `visit [-->]` to keep traversing. I'll add a `start` ability on root to kick off the descent, and have `collect` continue visiting after reporting:

```jac
node DataNode {
    has value: int = 0;
}

walker DataCollector {
    can start with Root entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can collect with DataNode entry {
        report here.value;  # Continues execution
        visit [-->];
    }
}

with entry {
    root ++> DataNode(value=1);
    result = root spawn DataCollector();
    all_values = result.reports;  # List of reported values
}
```

Now `start` fires at root and visits outward, and each DataNode reports its value then visits further, so `result.reports` gathers every value along the chain.

