```jac
def factorial(n: int) -> int {
    result = n;
    i = 2;
    while i < n {
        result *= i;
        i += 1;
    }
    return result;
}
```

You're right on both counts — starting from `result = n` breaks the n=0 case and the loop stops one short. Start at 1 and multiply every i from 2 through n inclusive:

```jac
def factorial(n: int) -> int {
    result = 1;
    i = 2;
    while i <= n {
        result *= i;
        i += 1;
    }
    return result;
}

with entry {
    for x in [0, 1, 5, 7, 10] {
        print(factorial(x));
    }
}
```

`factorial(0)` and `factorial(1)` both return 1; the loop runs `i <= n`.

