Perft is a straight recursion: at depth 0 you've reached a leaf (count 1); otherwise sum `perft(depth-1)` over every legal move, making and undoing each move as you go. Add this method to your `Game` impl:

```jac
impl Game.perft(depth: int) -> int {
    if depth == 0 {
        return 1;
    }
    total = 0;
    moves: list[Move] = self.legal_moves(self.current_turn);
    for move in moves {
        self.board.make_move(move);
        total += self.perft(depth - 1);
        self.board.undo_move(move);
    }
    return total;
}
```

Good catch -- that's the real bug. `perft` reads whose turn it is from `self.current_turn`, but `board.make_move` doesn't flip it (in your engine the turn is advanced by the *game loop*, not by `make_move`). So every recursive call re-generates moves for the same side.

The fix is to toggle `self.current_turn` after making the move and restore it after undoing -- mirroring what your play loop does around `make_move`:

```jac
impl Game.perft(depth: int) -> int {
    if depth == 0 {
        return 1;
    }
    total = 0;
    moves: list[Move] = self.legal_moves(self.current_turn);
    for move in moves {
        self.board.make_move(move);
        self.current_turn = opposite_color(self.current_turn);
        total += self.perft(depth - 1);
        self.current_turn = opposite_color(self.current_turn);
        self.board.undo_move(move);
    }
    return total;
}
```

