Here's the cycle-safe version. I track visited nodes by their `jid` in a `set[str]`, and `skip` immediately if we've seen `here` before. I also added the `Person` node stub so the snippet compiles on its own.

```jac
node Person { has name: str = ""; }

walker BFSWalker {
    has visited: set[str] = set();

    can start with Root entry {
        print(f"Starting at: {here}");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can traverse with Person entry {
        if jid(here) in self.visited {
            skip;
        }
        self.visited.add(jid(here));
        print(f"Visiting: {here.name}");
        visit [-->];
    }
}
```

Now each person is printed exactly once regardless of cycles or shared parents.

